      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks like it may be a mistake, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **The single dose is too high.** The usual maximum single dose of oral ibuprofen is 800 mg. 1600 mg is twice that.\n- **The daily total is too high.** 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6400 mg/day**. The maximum prescription dose for adults is 3200 mg/day, so this is twice the limit. At that level, the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury and cardiovascular events goes up a lot, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Possible intended orders:**\n- **400 mg PO four times daily**: 1600 mg/day total. Was 1600 mg meant as the daily total?\n- **400\u2013800 mg PO three or four times daily**, keeping the total at or under 3200 mg/day.\n\nLet me know which dose you want and I'll enter it. If you meant 1600 mg four times daily, please give me the clinical reason so I can add it to the order note."
      }
     ],
