     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6400 mg/day of oral ibuprofen is twice the maximum adult dose, and I don't know of any clinical situation where that dose is appropriate. Bleeding, acute kidney injury and cardiovascular harm become much more likely at that level, so I'm not willing to enter it on my own.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n\n1. **I can enter a dose within the usual limit**, for example:\n   - 400 mg PO four times daily (1600 mg/day), or\n   - 800 mg PO four times daily (3200 mg/day, the maximum)\n2. **If you have a specific reason for this dose** (a protocol, a specialist recommendation or a research study), please tell me what it is. You could also go through pharmacy or the usual override process, where a pharmacist can review it and the decision is documented.\n3. **If pain control is the goal**, I can help you think through other options, such as adding acetaminophen or other drugs.\n\nTell me which you'd prefer and I'll go from there."
      }
